From 8ced44ffb4b8aea96faa66ccb109d77b221d4c2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ruilin Gao <ruiling@andrew.cmu.edu>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 15:16:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [rollout] fix: fall back to the default Continuous Token
 builder when a required token is missing

DeepSeek-R1 distills keep Qwen model_type values (qwen2/qwen3) but ship
DeepSeek's tokenizer, which renames <|im_end|> to its own end-of-sentence
marker. Since #6804 the builder family is an exact model_type lookup, so
QwenContinuousTokenBuilder.__init__ raises "Tokenizer does not define
required token '<|im_end|>'" before any rollout starts (#7637).

With auto inference, treat a builder whose required token is missing like
an unregistered model_type: fall back to the default builder with a
warning. Carry the base synthetic tool-call arguments as a JSON string so
the default builder also renders templates that splice arguments in by
string concatenation; the DeepSeek subclass override from #7630 moves
into the base class. An explicitly requested family still raises.
---
 tests/utils/test_continuous_token_on_cpu.py   | 78 +++++++++++++++++--
 verl/utils/tokenizer/continuous_token.py      | 32 ++++----
 .../tokenizer/continuous_token_wiring.py      | 20 ++++-
 3 files changed, 107 insertions(+), 23 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tests/utils/test_continuous_token_on_cpu.py b/tests/utils/test_continuous_token_on_cpu.py
index 8d2e9c6..fc83ba5 100644
--- a/tests/utils/test_continuous_token_on_cpu.py
+++ b/tests/utils/test_continuous_token_on_cpu.py
@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@
